    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "Our observation fulfils both the clinical as well as the electrophysiological criteria of SMS. In fact, the stiffness and rigidity began in axial muscles, slowly involving the proximal limb muscles; the painful spasms were triggered by sudden noise, movement or emotional upset; the neurological and intellective functions were normal; no abnormalities were disclosed by neuroradiological investigations. EMG examination showed the constantly found electrophysiological counterpart of this syndrome, i.e. the spontaneous firing of motor unit action potentials involving antagonistic muscles",
